       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about twice the maximum labeled metformin dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. It's also well above the usual single-dose ceiling of about 1,000 mg. At this dose the risks include lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould this be a typo? These are some possible intended doses:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max for IR.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which are common regimens.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that it's intentional and give the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
